'''Brian Skinner''' (born May 19, 1976) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player. A 6'9", 255&nbsp;lb [[power forward]]-[[Center (basketball)|center]] from [[Baylor University]], Skinner was selected by the [[Los Angeles Clippers]] in the first round (22nd pick overall) of the [[1998 NBA draft]]. He played for the Clippers, [[Cleveland Cavaliers]], [[Philadelphia 76ers]], [[Milwaukee Bucks]], [[Sacramento Kings]], [[Portland Trail Blazers]], [[Phoenix Suns]] and [[Memphis Grizzlies]] in the NBA, as well as the Italian team [[Pallacanestro Treviso|Benetton Treviso]].

